    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i've tried the counselors and the therapy and everything. it's just like patching up a sinking ship with duct tape. at some point you just have to accept that the ship is gone. i don't want to 'find a foothold' in a life that feels this fundamentally wrong. it's like i'm just waiting for the clock to run out because the effort to keep existing is just... it's too much. don't you think it's exhausting to keep pretending things can actually get better when you know they won't?\n    it more honest to just admit that some",
